{
  "provider": "prismhr",
  "entity": "deduction_setup",
  "notes": [
    "getDeductions is the documented setup source (D-048): one DeductionSetup per employeeDeductions.deduction[] item, source_basis documented_assignment, id from (client, employee, deductionCode); a code repeated in one response adds the position with an unstable_id diagnostic. getVoluntaryRecurringDeductions is deselected: its records equal the type V records of getDeductions (8 of 8, D-081).",
    "Classification is held once on the client deduction code (D-047): deductionType sets category, tax_treatment and is_catch_up through prismhr.deduction_type, the same table as the company codes, so the link check finds no conflict. status is null with not_provided: getDeductions sends no status.",
    "Loans: a getEmployeeLoans or getRetirementLoans item whose loanId equals a getDeductions loanOrGarnishId fills that setup's loan part; any other loan makes its own setup (id adds 'loan' or 'retirement_loan' and the loanId, D-088; documented_assignment; code from deductionCode for employee loans; retirement loans send no code, so deduction_code_id is null and category is retirement_loan, documented by the route, raw_code 'retirementLoan', CANONICAL_MODEL 1.7). Live: loanOrGarnishId blank on 26 of 26 setups; 3 retirement loans for 1 employee.",
    "Garnishments: getGarnishmentDetails returned 403 for the demo user (6 of 6), so its rows come from the spec. A detail fills the garnishment part of the getDeductions setup with the same deductionCode, else makes its own setup (id adds 'garnishment' and the deductionCode, D-088). When details are refused, each setup classified as garnishment keeps its garnishment part null (not_provided) with source_unavailable; only an employee with no such setup whose checkForGarnishments says enrolled gets one presence_only setup (category garnishment, source_unavailable; D-048, D-088). Live: enrolled false on 2 of 2.",
    "Scheduled deductions (getScheduledDeductions, one-time or temporary): one setup each, documented_assignment; no id is sent, so the id adds 'scheduled' and the position, with unstable_id. Empty for 6 of 6 sampled employees.",
    "Arrears (getDeductionArrears): each entry is kept in the provider_extensions of the setup with the same deduction code (join; 26 of 26 live entries match the employee's LTD setup). An entry that matches no setup is not dropped: the Phase 5 adapter keeps it in Employee.provider_extensions.",
    "Dates documented as 'YYYY-DD-MM' on getEmployeeLoans (loanDate, startDate, stopDate; no live value, 6 of 6 empty) are read both ways (D-083), after the sentinel check on the raw value (D-025; 0000-01-01 is valid neither way): when only one of YYYY-MM-DD and YYYY-DD-MM gives a valid date, or both give the same date, that date is used; when both give different valid dates, the field is null with an unparseable_value diagnostic naming the raw value and the ambiguity, and the raw value is kept in provider_extensions; when neither is valid, null with unparseable_value. paymentHistory dates stay raw in provider_extensions."
  ],
  "fields": [
    {"route": ["/deductions/v1/getDeductions", "/employee/v1/getScheduledDeductions", "/deductions/v1/getEmployeeLoans", "/deductions/v1/getDeductionArrears", "/deductions/v1/getGarnishmentDetails", "/employee/v1/checkForGarnishments", "/benefits/v1/getRetirementLoans"], "field": "errorCode", "use": "excluded", "reason": "Response envelope; success is HTTP 200 with errorCode 0 (D-021)."},
    {"route": ["/deductions/v1/getDeductions", "/employee/v1/getScheduledDeductions", "/deductions/v1/getEmployeeLoans", "/deductions/v1/getDeductionArrears", "/deductions/v1/getGarnishmentDetails", "/employee/v1/checkForGarnishments", "/benefits/v1/getRetirementLoans"], "field": "errorMessage", "use": "excluded", "reason": "Response envelope (D-021)."},
    {"route": ["/deductions/v1/getDeductions", "/employee/v1/getScheduledDeductions", "/deductions/v1/getEmployeeLoans", "/deductions/v1/getDeductionArrears", "/deductions/v1/getGarnishmentDetails", "/employee/v1/checkForGarnishments", "/benefits/v1/getRetirementLoans"], "field": "extension.any", "use": "excluded", "reason": "Response envelope extension point; never filled in the samples."},

